<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <meta name="description" content="Terms of Service for RJ Printing Hub — campus thesis binding, book printing, and poster printing. Order, cancellation, and pickup/delivery terms." />
  <title>Terms of Service — RJ Printing Hub</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css?v=35" />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('partials/header') %>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__inner section__inner--narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__dot"></span>Legal</span>
      <h1>Terms of <span class="hl">Service</span></h1>
      <p class="section__subtitle">Last updated: <%= new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' }) %></p>

      <div class="legal-content">
        <p>
          These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of the RJ Printing Hub
          website and ordering system (the "Service"), operated for our campus
          printing and binding business. By creating an account, placing an order,
          or otherwise using the Service, you agree to these Terms.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
        <p>
          RJ Printing Hub provides thesis binding, book printing, poster printing,
          and related campus printing services. Orders are reviewed and processed
          by our team; some items are priced individually after review ("price on
          request") rather than shown as a fixed price up front.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Accounts</h2>
        <p>
          You need an account to place an order. You're responsible for keeping
          your login details secure and for all activity under your account. Let
          us know right away if you believe your account has been accessed without
          your permission.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Orders &amp; Pricing</h2>
        <p>
          Placing an order through the Service is a request to purchase, not a
          guaranteed sale — we may contact you to confirm specs, adjust pricing,
          or decline an order (for example, if a spec can't be produced as
          requested). Where an item shows "price on request," our team sets the
          final price after reviewing your order, and you'll be able to see that
          final price on your order page before it's fulfilled.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Cancellations</h2>
        <p>
          You may cancel an order yourself from your account within
          <strong>48 hours</strong> of placing it, as long as it hasn't already
          been marked delivered. After that 48-hour window, self-service
          cancellation is no longer available online — please contact us directly
          and we'll do our best to accommodate a late cancellation if production
          hasn't already started.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Fulfillment</h2>
        <p>
          At checkout you can choose pickup, local delivery, or shipping,
          depending on what's available for your order. Turnaround times shown on
          the site are estimates, not guarantees — urgent/rush orders are handled
          with priority where flagged, but delays can still happen due to volume,
          material availability, or circumstances outside our control.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Payment</h2>
        <p>
          Payment terms (method and timing) will be communicated to you directly
          for your order — either at checkout or by our team afterward, depending
          on how the order is priced. We'll always confirm the final price with
          you before completing your order.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Your Content</h2>
        <p>
          If you upload files, photos, or written material for us to print or
          bind, you confirm you have the right to use and reproduce that content.
          Please don't upload anything that infringes someone else's copyright or
          other rights.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          We aim to get every order right, but to the fullest extent permitted by
          law, RJ Printing Hub isn't liable for indirect, incidental, or
          consequential damages arising from use of the Service. Our total
          liability for any order is limited to the amount you paid for that
          order.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Changes to These Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms from time to time. If we make material
          changes, we'll update the "Last updated" date above. Continuing to use
          the Service after changes take effect means you accept the updated
          Terms.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these Terms? Reach out through our
          <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
        </p>

        <p class="legal-disclaimer">
          This page is a general template provided for informational purposes and
          doesn't constitute legal advice. It should be reviewed by a qualified
          professional before being relied on as your official Terms of Service.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
